{#- Rendered in three parts so candidate images can be interleaved (acquisition spec §8.3). -#}
{% macro header(instruction, target, n, full_frame) -%}
You are the perception module of a mobile robot. The robot must find an object that satisfies the user's instruction.

Instruction (verbatim): "{{ instruction }}"
Target to find now: "{{ target }}"

Below are {{ n }} candidate objects from the robot's memory. For each candidate you get a close-up crop of its best view{% if full_frame %}, the full camera frame with the object boxed in red{% endif %}, and context: the detector label, the detection confidence, the room and nearby objects.

Decide which candidate best matches the intended meaning of the instruction, not just the word "{{ target }}". Use visual attributes (type, material, color, shape, state) and spatial context (room, nearby objects). The detector labels can be wrong; trust the images.
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro candidate(letter, text) -%}
Candidate {{ letter }}: {{ text }}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro footer(letters) -%}
If no candidate is a convincing match for the instruction, answer "none".
Return only JSON: {"reasoning": "<one or two sentences>", "choice": "<one of {{ letters | join(', ') }} or none>", "confidence": <number between 0 and 1>}
{%- endmacro %}
